# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `wildcard_on_variant`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: `_` on a variant is a catch-all for every case no arm claims.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w14-wildcard_on_variant), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

variant Light
    red
    green
    blue

function name(l: Light) -> str
    return match l
        .red => "red"
        _    => "other"  #~ wildcard_on_variant

function main()
    print(name(.blue))
